{
  "_doc": "The stage spine. The run sequence previously existed ONLY as prose in agents/velt-orchestrator.md, so every tool that needed it re-derived or hardcoded it. This file is the single declarative source: which stages exist, who owns each, what each consumes and produces, which gates it must pass and with what exit contract, and what a per-stage review should look at. scripts/run-gate.mjs, scripts/stage-review.mjs and (later) the stage runner all read this. It describes BOTH build flows; `modes` scopes a stage to one of them. Nothing here changes behaviour on its own \u2014 it is a description, and golden/stage-review-calibration.mjs checks it against the orchestrator so it cannot drift.",
  "provenance": {
    "derivedFrom": "agents/velt-orchestrator.md Sequence 1-6, cross-checked against each gate script's own exit contract",
    "note": "Exit contracts are NOT uniform across this codebase \u2014 lint-primitives fails with 1, most gates with 2, console-health and browser-endpoint with 3, block-iter with 4/5. Each gate records its own."
  },
  "severity": {
    "blocking": "the orchestrator may not advance past this stage while the gate fails",
    "advisory": "recorded and surfaced; the human decides"
  },
  "lenses": {
    "ui": "rendered pixels \u2014 captures, diffs, mock scores",
    "functional": "does it actually behave \u2014 driven interactions, asserted states, console health",
    "code": "the source that was emitted \u2014 lints plus the checks lints cannot make"
  },
